          (the npm registry's "integrity" value, checked on download)
Files:    dist/mermaid.min.js (one file, sets the global "mermaid"), LICENSE -- unchanged copies. The bundle includes its
          own dependencies (d3, dagre, DOMPurify, langium, chevrotain and others, all MIT / ISC / Apache-2.0 / BSD).
          The notice block at the end of the file names only some of them; THIRD_PARTY lists all packages in mermaid's
          dependency tree (name, version, license) with their license texts (#4171). It is generated from the npm packages
          (versions resolved by npm at generation time, so it may name more packages than the minified file uses) and
          is not a copy from the tarball.
Loaded:   only when a page has a ```mermaid block; not in the service worker's precache. Runs with securityLevel
          "strict", no HTML labels.
Update:   download the new tarball, compare its sha512 with the registry's "integrity", copy the same files,
          regenerate THIRD_PARTY (mkdir /tmp/lic; cd /tmp/lic; npm install mermaid@<new version> --ignore-scripts
          --no-audit --no-fund; then, from the repository root,
          python3 -I tools/vendor_notices.py /tmp/lic/node_modules mermaid > static/vendor/mermaid/THIRD_PARTY),
          update this README and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
